{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>For Elohim has appointed me another seed instead of Abel.</b> Observe the expression ״זרע אחר תחת הבל״ — 'another seed instead of Abel' — for it was another seed in place of the seed from which Abel was sown; had Abel not been killed, Seth would not have been born, and this is the meaning of ״תחת הבל״ — literally in his place. And Scripture did not say 'a life instead of a life' (נפש תחת נפש), for had it said so, it would not have been literally instead of Abel. You already know that all matters of the work of Creation are wisdoms, and from this the masters of truth needed to draw from this passage a hint concerning Moses our master, upon him be peace — this is what they, of blessed memory, expounded: שג״ם — 'שגם' — this is Moses (שמשה), and his days were one hundred and twenty years, for so were his years. The word משה in itself embraces all three — Abel, Seth, Moses — and understand this. And he attributed this seed to the Holy One, blessed be He, because Abel too, and Seth, were in the likeness and image of the first man, who was made in the image of Elohim; therefore the name Elohim was mentioned in connection with him. And in saying <b>because Cain killed him</b>, he explains that Seth would not have come into being had Cain not killed Abel."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:10:25.242687095Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}